codemap 9
tour feature-hide-all-code
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The document toolbar's 'hide all code' hides the code of every step of the tour being read, leaving headers and notes; 'show all' shows every step's code again and also expands every collapsed step. The reader reaches for it to read a tour's notes and structure as prose without the code filling the screen. Steps shown inline under links keep their own state. It is one toggle (doc-code), not a pair: a run at 1600x1000 showed the toolbar as six identical bracketed buttons, 'hide all code' and 'show all code' side by side with nothing saying which state the tour was in. The toggle's label names what a press does next and it is drawn on while every step's code is hidden; with some steps hidden and some shown it is off and offers 'hide all code'. The palette keeps both commands (the document scenario runs '>collapse all' from it).

